goosebumps haunted Halloween takes us on  a new monster filled journey with slappy  the ventriloquist dummy getting up to  all kinds of mischief again  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers it's Jan here  and today I'm revealing the secret truth  about slappy and goosebumps - including  loads of freaky facts you need to know  about the movie make sure you stay to  the end to find out what goosebumps  author RL Stein appears in the sequel  and hit the bell to keep up to date with  all my new videos slappy the dummy is  one of the most popular characters in  the goosebumped series and although  author RL Stine was nearly 50 years old  in 1993 when slappy made his first  appearance and Night of the Living dummy  the inspiration for the creepy puppet  actually goes back many years earlier to  Stein's childhood as a young boy Stein  loved listening to his mother read him  The Adventures of Pinocchio not the  Disney animated version but the original  much creepier book that dark tale of a  wooden puppet which comes to life with  Stein's favorite book as a kid and left  a profound mark on him as an adult and  the classic British horror film dead of  night which Stein watched as a child was  also hugely important for Stein's  creation of slappy all those years later  by the way Stein says he enjoys writing  book starring slappy as he's a really  fun character to write because of how  much he insults everyone in fact Stein  even has a slappy dummy in his office  where he creates all his Goosebumps  books for the first goosebumps movie the  filmmakers wanted Slappy's face to look  like actor Jack flack because not only  did black star in the film as author RL  Stein but he also did the voice of  slappy however in haunted Halloween Jack  Black only makes a little cameo  appearance of Stein indeed according to  the real-life RL Stein initially black  wasn't even in the script for the  goosebumps equal because the actor was  too busy filming another horror movie  the house with a clock in 